## Hard rules (every agent must honor)

1. **Universal fonts only on native PPT text:** Calibri (body), Georgia (headers, take-home), Consolas (kickers/mono callouts). NO Crimson Pro / IBM Plex baked into native text. (Image-rendered slides MAY use any font baked into PNG.)
2. **All media EMBEDDED** in the .pptx — no linked files. Images via `add_picture()`. Videos via `add_movie(mime_type='video/mp4', poster_frame_image=...)`. Verify with `unzip -p OUT.pptx 'ppt/slides/_rels/*.xml.rels' | grep -c 'TargetMode="External"'` → must be 0.
3. **Claim-control:** synchrony **0.17 → 0.28 (>60%, Stier 2020)** ONLY — NOT 0.31→0.40. Predator demand **≈⅓ standing stock** ONLY — NOT "239%". SOK **$62.88/lb (1995) → $11–14/lb (2004)**. Last HG roe **2002**. P(SB<LRP)=**0.38** at zero catch. No "wolves" claim attributed to HG corpus specifically (wolves are in the Pacific Wild S6 video as visual texture; do not assert HG-corpus support).
4. **Take-home bookend:** *"Recovery is a moving target."* appears VERBATIM on S1 and S30. NOWHERE else in the deck.
5. **"Tipping point" deferred:** the phrase appears only in the S1 KICKER (citing session title) and in the S28 reframe slide. Adrian does not assert "this is a tipping point" anywhere else.
6. **Pacific Wild credit** on every video slide (S4, S6).
7. **Haida framing:** present-tense, sovereign nation. NEVER "stakeholders" or "human dimensions."
8. **kʼaaw framing:** *"the right and the ritual persisted; access did not."* Do not say "the kʼaaw economy persisted intact."

## Spine: 30 slides + 4 extras + 5 Q&A backups (read full detail in `v36_revised.md`)

Spine: S1 Title+thesis+take-home · S2 Haida Gwaii place · S3 Contrast water · S4 Herring arrive (video) · S5 Look closer cove scale+life history · S6 Wildlife (video) · S7 Predators came back · S8 Introduce Haida · S9 Archaeological record · **S10 Commercial fishery intro (seine fleet)** · **S11 Economics of herring (3 acts, roe value chart)** · S12 Three keystones summary · S13 THE PUZZLE · **S14 Zoom in: 2 contrasting locations + map** · S15 How we know · **S16 Model output (regional + local)** · **S17 Portfolio change (synchrony rose; integrated here, not in extras)** · S18 Productivity eroded · S19 Suspect 1 ocean · S20 Suspect 2 fishing · **S21 Two ultimate mechanisms (title card)** · S22 Recovered predators · S23 Lost elders / GWOF · **S24 Results summary** · S25 Solutions (allocate + re-couple) · S26 Co-governance · S27 Three lessons · S28 Tipping-point question reframe · S29 Reserved buffer · S30 Close bookend.

Extras (backup pool): X1 Portfolio theory (Markowitz/Schindler, 1950–67 window) · X2 Portfolio came apart (synchrony+1994 cliff) · X3 THE CLIMAX P=0.38 · X4 ACCESS TIPPING POINT 6 dimensions.

Q&A: B1 depensation pushback · B2 partial-rebound pushback · B3 EWS/CSD pushback · B4 cultural over-claim pushback · B5 Gladstone/kʼaaw pushback.

## Suggested swarm architecture (dispatch ALL agents in parallel where possible)

**Phase A — Asset Prep (1 agent, ~10 min):**
> "Prepare assets for v3.6 build. Read `/tmp/v36_revised.md`. Tasks: (1) ffmpeg-extract frames 0.1s and 5.0s from `~/Desktop/Herring_Talk_Clips/clips/v2_01_aerial_whitewater_spawn.mp4` → save to `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_assets_v36/s03_before.png` and `s03_after.png`. (2) Generate Haida placeholder PNG `s08_haida_PLACEHOLDER.png` via PIL (dark 3840×2160 with 'ASSET NEEDED — Adrian provides' text). (3) Confirm which slides can reuse `deck_assets/*.png` directly (S1 title, S9 baseline, S13 two-collapses, S15 ocean PDO, S20 fishing 4%/65%, S18 realized growth, X3 climax dfo biomass, B-slides as text-only). (4) List any slides needing fresh figures (S10 seine diagram, S11 roe-value chart from `figs/RebuildingPlan2024_*`, S14 zoom-in 2-coves panel, S16 model output, S17 synchrony matrix, S24 results summary). (5) Write `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_build_v36/ASSET_MANIFEST.md` listing source paths per slide. DO NOT modify build_v36.py."

**Phase B — Slide Builders (5 parallel agents, ~30 min each, run concurrently):**

Each builder agent gets a slug of slides + reference to `v36_revised.md` + asset manifest. They write a python-pptx slide-builder function per slide and append to `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_build_v36/slides_v36/sNN.py` (one file per slide, importable as a function `build(prs, prs_layout)` that takes a Presentation and adds one slide).

- **Builder 1 — cinematic opening (S1–S6):** title, Haida Gwaii place, water contrast, herring arrive video, look-closer life history, wildlife video. Heavy on full-bleed images + 2 video embeds.
- **Builder 2 — keystones build (S7–S12):** predators came back, Haida intro, archaeological, commercial fishery, economics, three keystones summary.
- **Builder 3 — puzzle + methods + zoom (S13–S18):** puzzle two-collapses, zoom 2 coves, methods grid, model output, portfolio change synchrony, productivity drained.
- **Builder 4 — suspects + mechanisms (S19–S24):** ocean, fishing, 2-mechanism title card, predators mechanism, lost elders/GWOF, results summary.
- **Builder 5 — close + extras + backups (S25–S30, X1–X4, B1–B5):** solutions, co-governance, lessons, tipping-point reframe, buffer, close bookend; the 4 backup-pool extras; the 5 Q&A pushback slides.

Builder agent prompt template:
> "Build slides {LIST} for the Royal Society herring talk v3.6 deck. Source content (verbatim — DO NOT INVENT): `/tmp/v36_revised.md`. Asset references: `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_build_v36/ASSET_MANIFEST.md`. Use python-pptx with universal fonts (Calibri/Georgia/Consolas) and the palette from existing `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_build_v36/build_v36.py` (C_DARK #0E0E0E, C_LIGHT #FBFAF7, C_RUST #D9714F, C_AMBER #CFA055, etc.). For each slide, write a function `build_sNN(prs)` that adds one 13.333×7.5 inch slide to the Presentation `prs`. Save each function as `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_build_v36/slides_v36/sNN.py`. Honor ALL hard rules (universal fonts, embedded media, claim-control numbers, take-home bookend, Pacific Wild credits on videos, Haida present-tense framing, kʼaaw 'right and ritual' wording). When complete, append to `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_build_v36/BUILD_LOG.md` with status per slide and any blockers. Speaker notes: copy the **Spoken** block verbatim from `v36_revised.md` into the slide's notes_slide.notes_text_frame."

**Phase C — Assembly (1 agent, after all builders complete, ~10 min):**
> "Assemble the v3.6 deck. Walk every `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/deck_build_v36/slides_v36/sNN.py` in spine order (S1–S30, then X1–X4, then B1–B5). Create a Presentation with 13.333×7.5 inch layout. Import each slide-builder function and call it on the prs. Save to `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/Herring_RoyalSociety_Stier_2026_v3.6_REVISED.pptx`. Generate PDF via `soffice --headless --convert-to pdf`. Append assembly summary to BUILD_LOG.md including: slide count, file size MB, embedded media count (`unzip -l OUT.pptx | grep ppt/media/`), and external-ref count (must be 0)."

**Phase D — QA Swarm (3 parallel agents, ~20 min, after assembly):**

- **QA Typography:** "Open the PDF at `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/Herring_RoyalSociety_Stier_2026_v3.6_REVISED.pdf`. Read every slide. Flag: text under 14pt (illegible at projection); low-contrast text; overflow/clipping; misaligned columns. Output: `QA_TYPOGRAPHY.md`."
- **QA Claim-Control:** "Audit every on-slide number / quote / citation against `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/docs/talk-model-claim-control-sheet.md` and `~/stier-2027-herring-metapopulation/talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/TALK_EVIDENCE_COVERAGE.md`. Flag any deviation. Output: `QA_CLAIM_CONTROL.md`."
- **QA Narrative + Portability:** "Trace the narrative arc S1 → S30. Flag any beat that doesn't land its purpose, any broken bridge, any missing take-home bookend at S30 (must verbatim match S1). Then run portability tests: unzip pptx and verify 0 external refs, all media in ppt/media/, file integrity (`unzip -tq`), and a jump-drive copy simulation (cp to /tmp, reopen via LibreOffice headless). Output: `QA_NARRATIVE_PORTABILITY.md`."

**Phase E — Patch + Final (orchestrator, ~15 min):**
Read the three QA reports. If any P1 issues: dispatch a targeted patch agent per slide. Re-render. Re-test portability. Final hand off with `V36_FINAL_STATUS.md` summary at the top of `Talk_Materials/`.

